.TH BAYEISHUUI-CPP 6 "October 2026" "Bayeishuui" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
bayeishuui-cpp \- Linux terminal Muay Thai duel (native C++17 implementation)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bayeishuui-cpp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bayeishuui-cpp
is the native C++17 build of Bayeishuui, a terminal-rendered martial-arts
duel focused on striking, footwork, range, stamina, and reading an
opponent's behaviour. The renderer uses ANSI true-colour and Unicode
terminal drawing to produce a perspective dojo floor, coloured fighter
silhouettes, health and stamina meters, range feedback, and live combat
messages. No third-party graphics libraries are required.
.PP
It shares combat rules, the sprite engine, and the Perfect Fighter policy
with
.BR bayeishuui-c (6);
the two are kept behaviourally aligned. At launch the game offers a
21-second Player 1 select: double-tap
.B Space
to control Player 1 manually; otherwise the built-in Perfect Fighter
heuristic takes Player 1 automatically. The campaign runs through the
Fighter Guild \(em 15 ranked opponents, 17 fights each.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A Linux/POSIX terminal supporting ANSI escape sequences and UTF-8, sized
at least 60 columns by 24 rows. The game must be run on an interactive
terminal (a TTY on both standard input and output).
.SH CONTROLS
.TS
l l.
W	Advance toward the opponent
A / D	Circle left / right
S	Retreat
Space	Strike (straight / close-range)
R	Teep
E	Round kick
G	Guard
J	Build ground control
K	Ground-and-pound
L	Attempt submission after building control
Q	Quit the bout
Escape	End an active Perfect Fighter session
.TE
.SH FILES
At session end a run-config file named
.I RANDOMTOKEN_YYYYMMDD_DURATION_ACCOUNT.cfg
is written in the current working directory. Existing files are never
overwritten.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal completion.
.TP
.B 2
Not running on an interactive terminal, or the terminal is smaller than
60x24.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bayeishuui-c (6)
